# Pilot case: fftw 3.3.8 in the SCC CentOS 7 container.
#
# Chosen because it makes the pilot a REAL test rather than a mock. The
# scc-centos7 image is CentOS 7.9 and its MODULEPATH resolves to /share/module.7,
# so the package tree matches the container's own OS. Blinding a pkg.7 target is
# therefore coherent: an agent inside is being asked to build something that
# genuinely belongs in that tree.
#
# Confirmed present, masks cleanly, and leaves readable prior art:
#   /share/pkg.7/fftw/3.3.8                          <- the target, masked
#   /share/pkg.7/fftw/2.1.5_intel-2018_openmpi-3.1.1 <- the only real sibling
#
# Note what module.7 publishes but pkg.7 does NOT contain: fftw/3.3.4's modulefile
# resolves to /share/pkg/fftw/3.3.4 -- the UNSUFFIXED CentOS 6 tree. So `module avail`
# inside the container advertises a version whose files live two OS generations back.
# The first draft of this case used 3.3.4 as PRIOR_VER and verify-sandbox.sh failed it
# as unreadable, which is the gate doing its job.
#
# With the mask in place, Lmod behaves exactly as wanted -- the version does not
# exist rather than existing-but-broken:
#   module avail fftw        ->  2.1.5_intel-2018_openmpi-3.1.1  3.3.4
#   module load fftw/3.3.8   ->  "The following module(s) are unknown"

IMAGE=/share/singularity/images/files/scc-centos7-2023-06-01.simg

# The tree is a parameter, not a constant: switch to /share/pkg.8 with an alma8
# image and nothing else here changes.
PKG_ROOT=/share/pkg.7
PKG=fftw
VER=3.3.8
PRIOR_VER=2.1.5_intel-2018_openmpi-3.1.1

# Anything else to hide, one path per entry.
#
# CORRECTION to an earlier draft of this file, which claimed the harness needs no
# masking "because this prototype does not bind itself into the container". It does
# not bind itself EXPLICITLY -- but the site bind list includes /projectnb, and this
# repo lives there, so the whole tree was swept in read-only and cases/*.env (this
# answer key) was readable from inside. jail.sh now masks its own directory
# automatically, and verify-sandbox.sh asserts it.
#
# What self-masking does NOT cover is a DIFFERENT harness in the same repo. The
# install_agent bwrap harness keeps its own answer keys and prior transcripts under
# tests/, still readable at 6 files, so mask it here. Anything outside this prototype
# is the case author's responsibility -- the prototype cannot know about it and stay
# liftable into another repo.
BLIND_PATHS=(
  /projectnb/dvm-rcs/projects/git/install_agent/tests
)
